On Tue, 16 Oct 2007 23:19:36 +0200, Carl <carlhnelson@gmail.com> wrote:

> Does anyone have any advice regarding late-game Nethack play without a
> luckstone?  As far as I can tell, the effects of not carrying a
> luckstone seem to be primarily limited to less divine assistance
> during prayer and lack of the to-hit modifier during combat.  There is
> also the problem of not getting a wish do to the phase of the moon
> (which has happened to me before).
>
> Other than those issues, are there any other things that I should
> consider?  What about zapping attack wands, does luck affect the
> chance to hit?

Yes, apparently, high luck is not that much needed. I don't know if it  
affects inventory curse (malignant aura)...
To-hit is not a problem with high level and sufficient skill, but in the  
late game that should be alright.

In my latest ascencion, I lost my luckstones (by swimming in the Lethe)  
just after going out of the Sanctum and didn't notice any real problem  
during the run (nothing worse than usual, that is).

Stones do not weight that much (10, as much as a dagger), so I'll probably  
not ditch my luckstone voluntarily but if I happen to lose it (eg nymph  
stealing it) when there's no time to go find it back (ie after waking  
Rodney), I'll probably won't go chasing the luckstone just for it...
Of course, you can also stack extra luckstone in convenient stashs close  
to the direct way up so that you can refill your inventory without  
spending too much time during the run.

